# Captured source frames: tens of megabytes of JPEG, re-fetchable with one command
# (`python -m workers.analytics.anpr.dataset capture …`, see README.md).
#
# The *crops* are committed instead, because they are what a human actually labelled and a number
# measured on a set nobody else can inspect is not a measurement.
frames/

# Contact sheets: derived from crops/ by one command
#   python -m workers.analytics.anpr.dataset sheet --condition day
# and 5 MB of PNG that nothing is measured from. The crops themselves are committed.
sheets/
